You may need to replace x with Old_x to ensure you're comparing properly with the old array list. 

Furthermore, for your NUnit test, you would need to include the necessary using statements (i.e., using NUnit.Framework;), as well as the [TestFixture] attribute for your test class, and [Test] attribute for your test methods to mark them as tests to be run by NUnit.--------------------These are the output assert statements corresponding to the comments that start with "@@@":

1. Assert that, given a specific x and arrList, if x is added to it at some position, then the index of x in the new array is always greater than or equal to some index of x in the same array.

